NNAAMMEE
     ppccaa995544xx — driver for PCA9548A I2C switch

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following line in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee ppccaa995544xx
           ddeevviiccee iiiiccmmuuxx
           ddeevviiccee iiiiccbbuuss

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           pca954x_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ppccaa995544xx driver supports the PCA9548A I2C bus switch and compatible
     chips such as TCA9548A.  It automatically connects an upstream I2C bus to
     one of several downstream buses as needed when slave devices on the down‐
     stream buses initiate I/O.  More information on the automatic switching
     behavior is available in iicmux(4).

FFDDTT CCOONNFFIIGGUURRAATTIIOONN
     On an FDT(4) based system, an ppccaa995544xx device node is defined as a child
     node of its upstream I2C bus.  The children of the ppccaa995544xx node are addi‐
     tional I2C buses, which will have their own I2C slave devices described
     in their child nodes.

     The ppccaa995544xx driver attaches to nodes where the _c_o_m_p_a_t_i_b_l_e property is set
     to one of

     ••   "nxp,pca9548"

     The ppccaa995544xx driver supports the following optional properties in addition
     to the standard I2C mux properties:

     _i_2_c_-_m_u_x_-_i_d_l_e_-_d_i_s_c_o_n_n_e_c_t  if defined, forces the switch to disconnect all
                              children in idle state.

HHIINNTTSS CCOONNFFIIGGUURRAATTIIOONN
     On a device.hints(5) based system, these values are configurable for
     ppccaa995544xx:

     _h_i_n_t_._p_c_a_9_5_4_x_._<_u_n_i_t_>_._a_t         The upstream iicbus(4) the ppccaa995544xx in‐
                                    stance is attached to.

     _h_i_n_t_._p_c_a_9_5_4_x_._<_u_n_i_t_>_._c_h_i_p___t_y_p_e  The type of the chip.  At present, only
                                    "pca9548" is supported.

     When configured via hints, the driver automatically adds an iicbus(4) in‐
     stance for every downstream bus supported by the chip.  There is cur‐
     rently no way to indicate used versus unused channels.

